6.1 Phishing

Phishing is a social-engineering attack in which an attacker impersonates a trusted person or organization to trick users into:

Revealing credentials
Opening malicious attachments
Clicking malicious links
Entering information into fake websites
Examples
Fake password-reset email
Fake Microsoft 365 login page
Fake invoice
Malicious attachment
Help Desk Response
Follow organizational reporting procedures.
Avoid opening suspicious links or attachments.
Determine whether credentials were entered.
Escalate to the security team if required.
Document the incident.
6.2 Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR)

EDR stands for Endpoint Detection and Response.

EDR technologies help organizations monitor endpoint activity, detect suspicious behavior, investigate threats, and support security response.

