6.3 Conditional Access

Conditional Access is a Microsoft Entra capability used to apply access controls based on conditions.

Conditions may include:

User
Device
Location
Application
Risk
Authentication requirements
Example
User signs in
 ↓
Conditions evaluated
 ↓
MFA required
 ↓
Access granted after verification
Interview Answer

Conditional Access allows organizations to apply access controls based on defined conditions such as user, device, location, application, or risk.

6.4 Multi-Factor Authentication

MFA uses two or more different authentication factor categories.

Something you know
Password
PIN
Something you have
Authenticator device/app
Security key
Something you are
Fingerprint
Facial recognition

Example:

Password
+
Authenticator App
=
MFA

Using a password and PIN alone normally represents only one factor category because both are "something you know."
